<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heligoland–Zanzibar Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Anglo-German Agreement of 1890</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Heligoland–Zanzibar Treaty was signed on 1 July 1890 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Germany recognised a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over Zanzibar and Pemba and British interests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> and gave up claims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witu">Witu</a>, while Britain ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> island of Heligoland to Germany. Zanzibar became a British protectorate later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heligoland-zanzibar-treaty.jpg" alt="Heligoland–Zanzibar Treaty" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-2005-0151,_%C3%9Cbergang_Helgolands_an_das_Deutsche_Reich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
